3:T10e1,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Where can I get an eye test in Tunbridge Wells?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"You can compare and book eye tests from multiple opticians in Tunbridge Wells through eyetest.co.uk. We list both NHS and private providers, including high-street chains like Boots Opticians and ASDA Opticians, as well as independent practices in the Kent area. Simply enter the postcode TN1 1YB to see all available options near you, compare prices, and book an appointment online in seconds."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much does an eye test cost in Tunbridge Wells?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Eye test prices in Tunbridge Wells typically range from free (NHS-funded) to around £39 for a private examination. Many people qualify for free NHS eye tests, including those over 60, under 16, those on certain benefits, and people with specific medical conditions. Budget opticians such as ASDA offer private tests from £20, while premium independent opticians may charge up to £79 for enhanced examinations with OCT scanning."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I get a free eye test in Tunbridge Wells?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, free NHS-funded eye tests are available at most opticians in Tunbridge Wells. You qualify if you are under 16 (or under 19 in full-time education), aged 60 or over, receiving certain means-tested benefits such as Universal Credit or Income Support, diagnosed with diabetes or glaucoma, or aged 40 or over with a close family member who has glaucoma. Use eyetest.co.uk to find NHS-registered opticians near TN1 1YB."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which opticians in Tunbridge Wells offer NHS eye tests?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Most opticians in Tunbridge Wells accept NHS patients, including Boots Opticians, ASDA Opticians, and many independent practices. You can filter for NHS availability when searching on eyetest.co.uk. All NHS-registered opticians must provide the same standard of clinical care, so the quality of your eye test will be consistent regardless of which practice you choose."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How often should I have an eye test?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The NHS and the College of Optometrists recommend an eye test every two years for most adults. However, you may need more frequent tests if you are over 70, have diabetes, have a family history of glaucoma or other eye conditions, wear contact lenses, or have been advised by your optometrist to return sooner. Children should have their eyes tested annually. Your optician in Tunbridge Wells can advise on the right frequency for your individual circumstances."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I book an eye test online in Tunbridge Wells?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, eyetest.co.uk makes it easy to book eye tests online in Tunbridge Wells. Simply enter your postcode or the postcode TN1 1YB, compare available appointments from multiple opticians, and book your preferred slot instantly. You will receive a confirmation email with all the details you need, including the practice address and what to bring to your appointment."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I need a referral for an eye test?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No, you do not need a GP referral to have an eye test in the UK. You can book directly with any optician in Tunbridge Wells through eyetest.co.uk or by contacting the practice. Eye tests are provided by qualified optometrists who are registered with the General Optical Council. If your optometrist finds anything that needs further investigation, they can refer you directly to a hospital eye specialist."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What should I bring to my eye test?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"When attending your eye test in Tunbridge Wells, bring your current glasses or contact lenses, any previous prescription you have, a list of medications you take, and your NHS exemption certificate or proof of benefits if you are claiming a free NHS test. If you wear contact lenses, you may be asked to remove them before certain tests, so bringing your glasses case is useful. Arrive a few minutes early to complete any registration paperwork."}}]}0:{"rsc":["$","$1","c",{"children":[[["$","$L2",null,{}],["$","main",null,{"className":"flex-1","children":[["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"WebPage\",\"name\":\"Eye Tests in Tunbridge Wells\",\"description\":\"Book eye tests in Royal Tunbridge Wells. Compare opticians on the High Street and the Pantiles.\",\"url\":\"https://www.eyetest.co.uk/locations/tunbridge-wells\",\"publisher\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"eyetest.co.uk\",\"url\":\"https://www.eyetest.co.uk\"},\"about\":{\"@type\":\"City\",\"name\":\"Tunbridge Wells\",\"containedInPlace\":{\"@type\":\"AdministrativeArea\",\"name\":\"Kent\"},\"geo\":{\"@type\":\"GeoCoordinates\",\"latitude\":51.1323,\"longitude\":0.2637}}}"}}],["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$3"}}],"$L4","$L5","$L6","$L7","$L8","$L9","$La","$Lb","$Lc","$Ld","$Le","$Lf","$L10","$L11","$L12","$L13"]}],"$L14"],["$L15"],"$L16"]}],"isPartial":false,"staleTime":300,"varyParams":null,"buildId":"ssq08EaNRRySny1_GDRUp"}
